{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27283830","formula":"C₇H₁₄N₄S₂","hill":"C7H14N4S2","elements":["H","C","N","S"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":14.0,"N":4.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"Methallibure"},"descriptions":{"en":"Metallibure (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name; also known as methallibure (USANTooltip United States Adopted Name, BANTooltip British Approved Name) or methallibur (German); brand names Aimax, Suisynchron, Turisynchron; former developmental codes ICI-33828, AY-61122, NSC-69536) is a medication which was introduced in 1973 and has been used in veterinary medicine to synchronize estrus. It was withdrawn in the United States and Europe due to teratogenicity and has been replaced with altrenogest (Regumate, Matrix), a progestin. The precise mechanism of action of metallibure is unknown."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":3003791,"mass":218.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C=C)NC(=S)NNC(=S)NC","inchikey":"CGFFKDRVHZIQHL-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-but-3-en-2-yl-3-(methylcarbamothioylamino)thiourea","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3003791","atoms":27,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.105,"y":2.709,"z":-0.504,"el":"S"},{"x":-3.193,"y":-2.023,"z":0.904,"el":"S"},{"x":1.319,"y":0.09,"z":0.232,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.816,"y":1.037,"z":0.202,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.334,"y":-0.162,"z":0.64,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.319,"y":0.315,"z":-0.497,"el":"N"},{"x":2.76,"y":-0.001,"z":0.089,"el":"C"},{"x":3.457,"y":0.4,"z":1.383,"el":"C"},{"x":3.1,"y":-1.409,"z":-0.303,"el":"C"},{"x":0.539,"y":1.209,"z":-0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":3.669,"y":-1.742,"z":-1.468,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.616,"y":-0.56,"z":0.313,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.671,"y":0.136,"z":-0.989,"el":"C"},{"x":3.085,"y":0.683,"z":-0.702,"el":"H"},{"x":0.843,"y":-0.755,"z":0.524,"el":"H"},{"x":4.546,"y":0.325,"z":1.282,"el":"H"},{"x":3.151,"y":-0.241,"z"